Wend (formerly Word Trails)
Privacy Policy
Wend · TLL Developers · Last updated: 17 November 2026

Wend, formerly called Word Trails ("the app") is a word puzzle game published by TLL Developers ("we"). This policy explains what data is processed when you use the app. The app does not require an account, and we do not ask for your name, email address or contacts.

1. Data stored on your device
Your progress (levels, daily results, streaks, statistics, coins, settings and in-progress puzzles) is stored only on your device. If Android backup is enabled on your phone, Android may include this data in your personal Google backup so it can be restored on a new device. We cannot access it.

2. Advertising (Google AdMob)
The app is free and shows ads served by Google AdMob. To serve and measure ads, Google may collect information such as your device's advertising ID, IP address, approximate location derived from it, device and app information, and ad interactions.

If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, the app asks for your consent through Google's User Messaging Platform before any ad is requested. You can change your choice at any time in Settings → Ad privacy choices. Elsewhere, you can limit personalised ads or reset your advertising ID in your Android settings.

More information: How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services.

3. Where your install came from
On its first launch, the app reads the Google Play Install Referrer once, to know which listing, cross-promotion or ad led to the install. This is a short referrer string (for example, which of our other apps or campaigns you came from); it does not contain your name, email address or contacts.

4. Crash reports, usage analytics and remote configuration (Firebase)
To keep the app stable and understand how it is played, the app uses Google Firebase Crashlytics (crash logs and diagnostics: stack trace, device model, OS and app version, app state at the time of a crash, and a random installation identifier) and Firebase Analytics (anonymous gameplay events such as a puzzle being started or completed, hints used, and app opens). The app also uses Firebase Remote Config to download settings that we can adjust without an app update (for example, how often ads appear or which features are enabled); the request includes your Firebase installation ID and basic device and app information. Google acts as our data processor for these Firebase services. These data are not used to identify you and are not sold.

4b. In-app purchases (Google Play)
The app offers an optional one-time purchase to remove ads. Payments are processed entirely by Google Play: we never see or store your card or payment details. Google Play tells the app whether the purchase is active on your account so the app can remove ads, and may share purchase information with us in aggregate or per order for accounting and support. You can restore the purchase on any device signed in to the same Google account, and manage or request a refund through Google Play.

5. Notifications
If you turn on the daily reminder, the app schedules local notifications on your device. No data is sent to us for this.

6. Sharing
When you tap Share, the app hands a short text (your time and a grid of coloured squares, never the solution) to the Android share sheet. What happens next depends on the app you choose.

7. Children
The app is intended for a general audience aged 13 and over and is not directed at children.

8. Data retention and your choices
Local data stays on your device until you use Settings → Reset progress, clear the app's storage or uninstall it. For data processed by Google, see Google's privacy policy at policies.google.com/privacy.

Data processed by third-party SDKs (as declared in Google Play Data safety)

This section lists, for Wend, the data processed by the third-party SDKs included in the app. It matches the Data safety form of the app on Google Play.

- Google AdMob (advertising): collects and shares with Google the advertising ID / app set ID and other device identifiers, an approximate location derived from your IP address, ad interactions (impressions, clicks) and diagnostics (such as app launches and performance). Purposes: advertising, ad measurement and analytics, and fraud prevention and security. We do not receive your name or contact details from AdMob.
- Firebase Analytics (Google): app interactions (events and screens viewed), the Firebase installation ID / device identifiers, and basic device and app information. Purposes: analytics and app functionality.
- Firebase Remote Config (Google): the Firebase installation ID and basic device and app information, used to deliver app settings. Purpose: app functionality.
- Google Play Billing (Google): purchase status for the remove-ads purchase, handled by Google Play. Purpose: app functionality.
- Firebase Crashlytics (Google): crash logs and diagnostics (stack trace, device model, Android and app version, a random installation ID). Purposes: analytics and app stability.

Ad choices: you can reset or delete your advertising ID and opt out of ads personalisation in Android Settings > Google > Ads.
Security: data sent to these services travels encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS).
Data deletion: the app has no user accounts. Data stored on your device is deleted by uninstalling the app or clearing its data; for data held by Google (advertising ID, analytics), reset your advertising ID as described above or write to tll.developers.apps@gmail.com and we will help with the request.

